Input: {"question": "When was Princess Elisabeth of Thurn and Taxis born?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d00", "start": 0, "end": 393, "text": "Princess Elisabeth Helene of Thurn and Taxis Princess Elisabeth Helene of Thurn and Taxis () (15 December 1903, Regensburg, Kingdom of Bavaria – 22 October 1976, Munich, Bavaria, Germany) was a Princess of Thurn and Taxis by birth and a Princess and Duchess of Saxony, Margravine of Meissen, and titular Queen consort of Saxony through her marriage to Friedrich Christian, Margrave of Meissen."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d00", "start": 394, "end": 523, "text": "Elisabeth was the sixth child of Albert, 8th Prince of Thurn and Taxis and his wife Archduchess Margarethe Klementine of Austria."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d00", "start": 524, "end": 633, "text": "Elisabeth married Prince Friedrich Christian of Saxony, second eldest child and son of Frederick Augustus III"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "by her nickname, TNT."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 22, "end": 146, "text": "Elisabeth was born on 24 March 1982 at the family palace, Schloss Thurn und Taxis, 500-room 8th-century abbey in Regensburg."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 147, "end": 323, "text": "She is the middle child of Johannes, 11th Prince of Thurn and Taxis (5 June 1926 – 14 December 1990) and Gloria Princess of Thurn and Taxis (née Gräfin von Schönburg-Glauchau)."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 324, "end": 475, "text": "She has an older sister, Maria Theresia (born 28 November 1980), and a younger brother, Albert (born 24 June 1983), who succeeded their father in 1990."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 476, "end": 587, "text": "The former German princely House of Thurn and Taxis is one of Germany's wealthiest and most prominent families."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d01", "start": 588, "end": 591, "text": "Her"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d02", "start": 0, "end": 5, "text": "life."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d02", "start": 6, "end": 140, "text": "Her husband Miguel eventually remarried on 8 November 1893 in Kleinheubach to Princess Maria Theresa of Löwenstein-Wertheim-Rosenberg."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d02", "start": 141, "end": 598, "text": "Princess Elisabeth of Thurn and Taxis Princess Elisabeth of Thurn and Taxis (German: \"Elisabeth Maria Maximiliana\") (28 May 1860, Dresden, Kingdom of Saxony – 7 February 1881, Ödenburg, Austrian Empire) Elisabeth was a Princess of Thurn and Taxis by birth and an Infanta of Portugal, Princess of Braganza, and titular Queen consort of Portugal through her marriage to Miguel, Duke of Braganza, Miguelist claimant to the throne of Portugal from 1866 to 1920."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d02", "start": 599, "end": 652, "text": "Elisabeth was the second eldest child and daughter of"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 0, "end": 167, "text": "German : Elisabeth Maria Maximiliana ; [ citation needed ] 28 May 1860 – 7 February 1881 ) was the Duchess of Braganza and wife of Miguel Januário , Duke of Braganza ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 168, "end": 202, "text": "This article has multiple issues ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 203, "end": 268, "text": "Please help improve it or discuss these issues on the talk page ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 269, "end": 375, "text": "( Learn how and when to remove these messages ) This article needs additional citations for verification ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 376, "end": 451, "text": "( April 2023 ) This article relies largely or entirely on a single source ."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 452, "end": 518, "text": "( April 2023 ) Quick Facts Elisabeth of Thurn and Taxis , Born ..."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d03", "start": 519, "end": 528, "text": "Elisabeth"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d04", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "of Bavaria 7 ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d04", "start": 15, "end": 48, "text": "Princess Ludovika of Bavaria 15 ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d04", "start": 49, "end": 164, "text": "Princess Caroline of Baden References [ edit ] Manuel de Mello Corrêa ( eds ) : Anuário since Nobreza de Portugal ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d04", "start": 165, "end": 215, "text": "Instituto Português de Heráldica , Lisboa , 1985 ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d04", "start": 216, "end": 550, "text": "Princess Elisabeth of Thurn and Taxis ( 1860–1881 ) House of Thurn and Taxis Cadet branch of the House of Tassis Born : 28 May 1860 Died : 7 February 1881 Titles in pretence Preceded by Adelaide of Löwenstein — TITULAR — Queen consort of Portugal Miguelist line 17 October 1877–7 February 1881 Succeeded by Maria Theresa of Löwenstein"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0317-1d81337f2110:d05", "start": 0, "end": 10, "text": "a friend ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "r